{"input_tokens":64120,"output_tokens":3608,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify or fix the `first-done`-before-`second-done` assertion: since the lock releases before `first-done` is sent, assert only the lock-held invariant (second cannot complete while first holds the lock — already covered by the negative poll) and drop or synchronize the post-release global-order check that reproduces the original race.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["marker.py:51-54: `with _marker_lock(lock_path): with open(marker_path, 'a'): pass` — lock released on context exit, before write_marker returns","test:33-34: `marker.write_marker(ticket_dir); events.send('first-done')` — first-done is sent after lock release","test:119-122 assert first-done then second-done","Symptom: actual order was `first-has-lock, second-done, first-done` — the same post-release window exists cross-process"],"finding":"The fixed test's assertion that `first-done` precedes `second-done` is a residual ordering race that the thread->process change does not remove: write_marker releases the lock at `_marker_lock` context exit (marker.py:51-54) BEFORE the worker sends `first-done` (test:34), so the already-blocked second process can acquire the lock and emit `second-done` first — reproducing the original symptom.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fea235f49bf2c6c04","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 'documents the failing order first-has-lock, second-done, first-done'; test lines 119-122","norm_id":"n0795ed0a04f8c41a","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Second process wins the scheduler race after lock release but before first process sends first-done"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have the worker signal an event immediately after acquiring the lock and before release, and assert the second process is blocked during the hold (the `assert not event_rx.poll(timeout=0.2)` already does this). Remove the assertion requiring `first-done` strictly before `second-done`, or add explicit synchronization that sends `first-done` before releasing the lock.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the fixed cross-process test behaves on non-POSIX venues (Windows / no-flock platforms): guard/skip the flock-serialization assertion via platform detection, and confirm the process-spawn mechanism does not rely on os.fork.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'test a POSIX flock critical section' and test name 'test_marker_lock_serializes_posix_access'","Reproduction only cites Linux venues (ubuntu py3.11, Python 3.12 default suite)","Support matrix includes Windows platform, where os.fork is unavailable (multiprocessing uses spawn) and fcntl.flock does not exist","AC 'Marker no-primitive fallback tests continue to pass' implies a no-primitive path exists for platforms lacking flock"],"finding":"The fix mandates 'two independent processes contending on the marker lock file' with POSIX flock semantics (test named test_marker_lock_serializes_posix_access) but does not state how this test behaves on non-POSIX venues in the support matrix, where fork and flock are unavailable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2cf3180df40380fb","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: 'The fixed test exercises two independent processes contending on the marker lock file' / 'uses explicit inter-process synchronization'","norm_id":"n69136c843a2895ab","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows CI (GitHub Actions windows runner): if the new test spawns processes via os.fork or asserts flock behavior unconditionally, the test errors/crashes rather than skipping — the suite fails on a platform the harness must support","A platform using the no-primitive marker fallback: two processes may not serialize, so the posix-serialization assertion would fail or must be guarded/skipped"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a criterion that the test is skipped (or asserts the no-primitive contract) when fcntl.flock is unavailable, and use a spawn-safe process launch (e.g. subprocess or multiprocessing with an explicit spawn context) rather than os.fork so the test is inert-but-correct on Windows.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the diagnosis with the snapshot: confirm whether the failing threaded oracle existed in the patch set under review (e.g., patchset 1 of change 2888) and cite that revision, since the current tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py already uses multiprocessing.get_context('spawn') with two ctx.Process workers and no threading.Thread.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py uses threading.Thread inside one Python process to test a POSIX flock critical section'","Snapshot lines 87-101: ctx = multip